How This Project Was Made

I started this project because I couldn't find arcade skins that fit the games I wanted to play on the go, and I wanted to share something useful with the community.
• Where AI was used: When I first started, I didn't have a background in coding or graphic design. I used AI early on as a learning aid to help generate initial base PNGs, colorway variations, and starter info.json templates.
• Where the real work went (90%+ human effort): Every layout, button placement, Dynamic Island safe zone, D-pad overshoot zone, and colorway choice was designed by me. As the project grew past 3,000+ skins and 200+ hours of work, I learned how to write, edit, and run my own custom scripts, compilers, and verifiers to patch button mappings (like the Manic EMU 2.0.2 overhaul) and ensure consistent quality across iPhone and iPad.
• Hand-Tested: Every layout style is tested on real hardware with actual arcade ROMs before release so you don't have to deal with broken inputs or overlapping controls.
